WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.030 --> 00:00:08.180
See the books at a glance, then post a manual entry with balanced debits and credits.

2
00:00:08.180 --> 00:00:17.390
Accounting opens on the overview: cash in the banks, what tenants owe, what you owe suppliers and the result of the year.

3
00:00:17.390 --> 00:00:25.940
Rent invoices, payments, payroll and purchases post here by themselves. You only post what the office does not know about.

4
00:00:25.940 --> 00:00:34.800
Open the Journal to see every entry, with a link back to the invoice or receipt that made it.

5
00:00:34.800 --> 00:00:38.360
Choose New entry.

6
00:00:38.360 --> 00:00:46.450
Describe the entry. The date is today; change it if the entry belongs to another day.

7
00:00:46.450 --> 00:00:51.490
On the first line, choose the expense account: bank charges.

8
00:00:51.490 --> 00:00:54.540
And the amount as a debit.

9
00:00:54.540 --> 00:01:00.060
On the second line, the bank account the money left from.

10
00:01:00.060 --> 00:01:06.650
The same amount as a credit. The totals underneath must balance before you can post.

11
00:01:06.650 --> 00:01:12.110
Need more lines? Add a line, for example to split VAT.

12
00:01:12.110 --> 00:01:22.340
Post the entry. It gets its own number, and a posted entry is never edited: to undo it, you reverse it.
